{"name":"Marina","hex":"#5a88c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Marina","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Fabaceae – false prairie clovers, of southern North America."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Latin.","A transliteration of the Russian female given name Марина (Marina)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Marina"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marina","blocks":[{"text":"A marina is a dock or area of water with piers and moorings for securing and parking yachts and small boats. A marina differs from a port in that a marina is not designed to handle large passenger ships or freighters, and is often for leisure boating activities such as yachting, sailing and boat tours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg/330px-Guarda-corpo_da_Avenida_Portugal_-_Rio_de_Janeiro_-_20220923024517.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina","wikidata":"Q721207"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg/500px-New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg/1280px-New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg/500px-New_River_South_Fork_%2830392885610%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marina in Fort Lauderdale, Florida","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_River_South_Fork_(30392885610).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://